// Three-tier concurrency surface: `thread`, `spawn`, `job`.  All three
// take a `unit()` closure, return a `*Thread` handle, and are joined via
// `join(h)`.  See CONCURRENCY.md for the full design.
//
// MVP: all three are pthread-backed.  The real fiber and job runtimes
// arrive later without changing the surface.

unit main() {
    *Thread t1 = thread(unit() { log(1); });
    join(t1);

    *Thread t2 = spawn(unit() { log(2); });
    join(t2);

    *Thread t3 = job(unit() { log(3); });
    join(t3);

    log(0);
}
